'''Drain Vitality''' is a [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|dragon shout]] introduced in the [[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]] [[Skyrim:Add-ons|add-on]] that drains stamina, magicka, and health from an enemy. The [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragons]] added by Dawnguard, Revered and Legendary, each have their own version of this shout. Their versions of the shout drain 5 and 7 stamina, magicka, and health per second, respectively, for a duration of 20 seconds.

{{NewLeft}}

==Notes==
* Drain Vitality is not affected by Spell Absorption, Resist Magic, or Cure Poison.
* There are another four versions of the Shout in addition to the three already mentioned. The four shouts, with consecutive editor ids (<small><code>DLC1DragonDrainVitalityShout02</code>, 03, 04, and 05</small>), deal 1, 2, 3, and 4 damage per second, respectively, for 20 seconds. The two shouts used by the Revered and Legendary dragons have editor ids of <small><code>DLC1DragonDrainVitalityShout06</code></small> and <small><code>DLC1DragonDrainVitalityShout07</code></small>, respectively.
* With sufficiently shortened cooldown (Amulet of Talos and Blessing of Talos, or abusing the [[Skyrim:Fortify Restoration|fortify restoration glitch]]), it is possible to stack the effects of multiple Drain Vitality Shouts together, which will cause faster and faster resource draining on the affected.
**Stacked Drain Vitality shouts can cause Dragons to be unable to use their breath attacks and Dwarven Centurions to be unable to use their steam attack. This is because both attacks require magicka to use, and the stacked shouts will drain their reserves completely. Vampires will also be unable to use spells and their Vampiric Drain. Continuing to stack the shout will guarantee an empty magicka and stamina pool to the ones affected.
* This shout appears in ''[[Legends:Legends|Legends]]'' as the {{Card|Drain Vitality}} card. For the alternate art version of this card, the shout's effects appear as a red and black aura rather than the usual purple effect.

